; Swordfighter (Marth) — AttackLibrary.
; Frame data sourced from Super Smash Bros. Ultimate (Kurogane Hammer database)
; and Melee community documentation. Marth is the definitive spacing character.
;
; TIPPER MECHANIC
;   ForwardTilt and ForwardSmash each have TWO hitboxes in their Hitboxes array:
;     Hitboxes[0] = tipper   (sword TIP  — high damage, high knockback, KILLS)
;     Hitboxes[1] = sourspot (sword BASE — low damage, low knockback, combo only)
;   Scene setup: add two Area2D hitbox nodes per tipped move.
;     ForwardTiltTipper  — position at sword tip (furthest from character)
;     ForwardTiltBase    — position along sword length (closer to character)
;   The tipper (HitboxNodeName) has PRIORITY: AttackState calls SuppressTarget()
;   on the sourspot if the tipper connects, preventing double-hits.
;
; Kit philosophy:
;   Jab1/2  : fast, low-commitment. Resets to neutral or links into tilt.
;   ForwardTilt: frame 8 poke. Tipper combos at low %, sourspot is safe-on-shield.
;   UpTilt   : frame 6 anti-air. Juggles into re-tilt or ForwardAir strings.
;   ForwardSmash: frame 10 tipper = kill move; sourspot = combo starter below 80%.
;   NeutralAir: long-lasting aerial. Covers landing and platform pressure.
;   ForwardAir: frame 6. Forward air is the primary combo aerial (Dancing Blade idea).
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AttackLibrary" load_steps=24 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Scripts/Character/Combat/AttackLibrary.cs" id="Script_AttackLibrary"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Scripts/Character/Combat/AttackData.cs"    id="Script_AttackData"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Scripts/Character/Combat/HitboxData.cs"    id="Script_HitboxData"]

; ── Jab 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
